/-!
# `SingularFlatAxioms` at every `E_{≥0}`-manifold, singular flat spacetimes, and the measures

Target `T-ett-singular-sfa`. Cited, **unmarked** (SCOPE): `def:singular_spacetime` —
`ETT.tex:1500`; `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` — `ETT.tex:1508`;
`prop:mesure_admissible` — `ETT.tex:1726`. For a singular `(Isom(𝐌³), 𝐌³)`-manifold `M` (DEC-25),
Hausdorff and second countable, and every absolutely minimal causality `C` with an isomorphic chart
at each point over the family `E_{≥0}` (`IsoChartsCoverDEC25 … massAModelCausality`; the natural
causality is one), `C` satisfies `Causal.Causality.SingularFlatAxioms` for `sing_α(M)` read through
the `X_A`-charts (`SFALocal.sing M`), with no field left; on a connected `M` it is
`Causal.Causality.SingularFlatSpacetime`, the library's form of `def:singular_spacetime`. Then
`prop:mesure_admissible` and `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` (DEC-18) hold at every
strongly causal such `M`, with no hypothesis left beyond the readings.

> Let $A$ be a subset of $\RR_+$. An $\mass{A}$-spacetime is a connected $\E^{1,2}_A$-manifold
> endowed with the causality generated by its $X_A$-atlas and by the causalities of $X$ and of the
> $(X_\alpha)_{\alpha\geq 0}$. We simply say singular flat spacetime when $A=\RR_+$.
> (`def:singular_spacetime`, `ETT.tex:1500–1507`)

> A singular flat spacetime is therefore a differential manifold and satisfies all the hypotheses
> of Geroch's Theorem \ref{theo:geroch}. (`rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore`,
> `ETT.tex:1508–1511`)

> Let $M$ be a strongly causal $\mass{\geq 0}$-manifold. Then $M$ carries a measure $\mu_-$
> admissible in the past and a measure $\mu_+$ admissible in the future.
> (`prop:mesure_admissible`, `ETT.tex:1726–1728`)

## What is proved

* **The assembly** (`singularFlatAxioms`): `SingularFlatAxioms (SFALocal.sing M)` at every T2,
  second countable `E_{≥0}`-manifold for every absolutely minimal `C` with an isomorphic chart at
  each point, by one `SFABTZ.singularFlatAxioms_iff_lines` fed with `SFALine.line` and
  `SFAMassiveLine.massive_line`. Mixed manifolds (BTZ and massive points) included.
* **`def:singular_spacetime`, read** (`singularFlatSpacetime`, `singularFlatSpacetime_iff`): such
  a `C` is a `SingularFlatSpacetime` iff `M` is connected.
* **The natural causality** (`singularFlatAxioms_of_isAtlasCausalityDEC25`,
  `singularFlatSpacetime_of_isAtlasCausalityDEC25`), and its existence form
  (`exists_singularFlatAxioms`): every T2, second countable `E_{≥0}`-manifold carries a natural
  causality satisfying `SingularFlatAxioms`, the only absolutely minimal causality with an
  isomorphic chart at each point.
* **Sub-families**: `E₀`-manifolds (`singularFlatSpacetime_e0`, out of the assembly through
  `SFALocal.sing_eq_of_e0Covered`; the `SingularFlatAxioms` form is `SFALine.singularFlatAxioms_e0`)
  and `E_{>0}`-manifolds (`singularFlatSpacetime_of_massive`, from
  `SFAMassiveLine.singularFlatAxioms_of_massive`).
* **The measures, unconditional**: `mesure_admissible`, `geroch_hypotheses` (every strongly causal
  T2, second countable `E_{≥0}`-manifold), `mesure_admissible_of_isAtlasCausalityDEC25`,
  `geroch_hypotheses_of_isAtlasCausalityDEC25` (its natural causality);
  `MeasuresManifolds.e0Manifold_mesure_admissible_natural`,
  `MeasuresManifolds.e0Manifold_geroch_hypotheses_natural` (`E₀`-manifolds; T-ett-sfa-line-e0's
  AUDIT-1).
* **Witnesses** (kb/0011), each conclusion out of this file's theorems: `nonvacuous_e0` (`E₀`,
  `sing₀ = axis ≠ ∅`), `nonvacuous_e0_natural`, `nonvacuous_e0Manifold`, `nonvacuous_epi`
  (`E_π`, `sing_π = line ≠ ∅`), `nonvacuous_epi_massive` (`E_π` as an `E_{>0}`-manifold), and
  the conclusions of `geroch_hypotheses` at both (`nonvacuous_e0_geroch`, `nonvacuous_epi_geroch`).
* **A lemma the witness needs**: `E_κ`, `κ > 0`, is connected (`massive_connectedSpace`, through
  `preconnectedSpace_of_geodesicSpace`: a geodesic space is preconnected); the library had no
  `ConnectedSpace` for `E_κ`.

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper | here |
|---|---|
| a connected `E^{1,2}_A`-manifold, `A = ℝ₊` (l.1502, 1506) | ⚠ special case, read (DEC-25): the family `E_{≥0}` (`A ⊆ ℝ₊` is the models allowed, not required); `[SingularGXStructure (Flat.isom 2) (Minkowski 2) M]`, singular points in `X_A`-charts into the family `E_{≥0}` (`MassACovered`, implied by `IsoChartsCoverDEC25`); connectedness ✓ carried by the `SingularFlatSpacetime` forms only (`[ConnectedSpace M]`, and `singularFlatSpacetime_iff`) |
| « manifold », « spacetime »: Hausdorff, second countable (`ETT.tex:255`) | ✓ carried: `[T2Space M] [SecondCountableTopology M]` (fields of `SingularFlatAxioms`) |
| « the causality generated by its `X_A`-atlas and by the causalities of `X` and of the `X_α` » (l.1502–1504) | ⚠ read (OQ-18): the natural causality `IsAtlasCausalityDEC25` (`…_of_isAtlasCausalityDEC25`, `exists_singularFlatAxioms`); ⚠ weakened in the main forms: any absolutely minimal `C` with an isomorphic chart at each point (`IsoChartsCoverDEC25`), which is the natural one when it exists (`EModelsBPrime.massA_causalite_models`) |
| `E₀` (l.1330), `Isom(𝔼^{1,2})` | ⚠ read: `Causal.E0` (OQ-34, OQ-35), `Flat.isom 2 = SO₀(1,2) ⋉ ℝ³` (OQ-82) |
| « a differential manifold » (l.1509) | not formalized (no differentiable structure in the library) |
| strongly causal (l.1726) | ✓ carried, DEC-7's `StronglyCausal` |
| strongly causal, in `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore` | ⚠ strengthened: assumed (DEC-18) |
| « all the hypotheses of Geroch's Theorem » | ✓ the conjunction of the strict `SingularFlatAxioms.geroch_hypotheses` |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **Why unmarked.** The three rows rest on the readings DEC-25 (the manifolds), OQ-18 (« the
  causality generated by its `X_A`-atlas »), OQ-34/OQ-35 (`E₀`) and OQ-82 (the group);
  `rem:singular_flat_spacetime_therefore`'s « differential manifold » is not formalized and its
  strong causality is assumed (DEC-18). `def:singular_spacetime` is a definition: the library
  abstracts it as `SingularFlatSpacetime`, and this file proves the abstraction is implied by the
  definition read through DEC-25 and OQ-18, for `A = ℝ₊` (and for `A = {0}`, `A = (0, ∞)`).
* **`sing_α(M)`** is `SFALocal.sing M α` (brunswic2021cauchy Cor. 1.5), as in `Causal.SFALocal`.
* **Witnesses.** `E₀` has BTZ points only and `E_π` massive points only; no witness has points of
  both kinds (no disjoint union of singular structures in the library, `Causal.SFALocal` SCOPE).
* **Not here**: the rows that consume `SingularFlatAxioms` at `M` (T-ett-singular-rows,
  T-ett-singular-rows-geroch, T-ett-singular-rows-local); the docstrings that still call this
  target future (T-ett-docstrings-sing0).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`. Imports the strict
`Causal.Port.SFABTZ`, `Causal.Port.SFALine`, `Causal.Port.SFAMassiveLine`,
`Causal.Remarks.MeasuresManifolds` and `Causal.Remarks.EModelsBPrime` (the existence of the natural
causality, `EModelsBPrime.massA_causalite_models`, for `exists_singularFlatAxioms`, and the `E_π`
witness's naturality).
